  "title": "Federal Government Weekly Delta — September 4–11, 2026",
  "question": "What materially changed across official U.S. federal sources from September 4 through September 11, 2026 after the targeted weekly was corrected with a broader publisher walk?",
  "bluf": "The September 4-11 sweep found material movement across citizenship and apportionment rules, Canada tariff scope, Defense Production Act delegations, Iran sanctions, spending-transparency law, bank examination thresholds, courts, energy finance, military procurement, and federal delivery. A later Wave 3 publisher walk corrected the targeted weekly by adding NRC, FERC, NARA, SBA, EXIM, DFC, CISA, DOJ, CMS, CBP, FEMA, CDC, NNSA, CHIPS, SAMHSA, NLRB, and FEC objects. Proposal, approval, award, obligation, payment, delivery, operation, and observed result remain separate.",
  "evidence_cutoff": "2026-09-11T16:01:37-04:00",
  "use_note": "Frozen Workbench evidence through 2026-09-11 16:01:37 EDT. Read the Wave 3 merge before the earlier ranked synthesis. Refresh later states at official sources and preserve legal, funding, approval, delivery, operating, and observed-effect clocks. No Chronicle promotion or exhaustive government census is claimed.",
